1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:03,003
Hackers are inside the Air Force's
flagship cloud,

2
00:00:03,023 --> 00:00:04,809
and nobody knows what they took.

3
00:00:05,049 --> 00:00:06,230
It's called Cloud One,

4
00:00:06,250 --> 00:00:08,194
and it hosts systems that handle air

5
00:00:08,214 --> 00:00:10,650
defense radar data from across North
America.

6
00:00:10,890 --> 00:00:14,281
Sources say it was found during an
upgrade, updates are blocked,

7
00:00:14,301 --> 00:00:16,147
and the Air Force won't confirm it.

8
00:00:16,387 --> 00:00:17,678
This is at least the seventh

9
00:00:17,698 --> 00:00:19,737
recent hack of the United States
government.

10
00:00:19,977 --> 00:00:20,645
In September,

11
00:00:20,665 --> 00:00:22,393
hackers broke into the FBI's jobs

12
00:00:22,413 --> 00:00:24,458
portal and got Social Security numbers.

13
00:00:24,698 --> 00:00:28,184
The Pentagon's personnel system was open
to intruders for months,

14
00:00:28,204 --> 00:00:30,180
exposing nearly three million people.

15
00:00:30,420 --> 00:00:31,094
In October,

16
00:00:31,114 --> 00:00:32,546
data on more than forty

17
00:00:32,566 --> 00:00:35,576
thousand Homeland Security employees was
leaked,

18
00:00:35,596 --> 00:00:37,217
including some undercover.

19
00:00:37,456 --> 00:00:40,577
And this week, hackers hit the CIA and two
other spy agencies,

20
00:00:40,597 --> 00:00:42,806
then the Treasury's financial crimes
bureau.

21
00:00:43,046 --> 00:00:45,399
One source says investigators suspect an
AI

22
00:00:45,419 --> 00:00:47,496
hacking tool in the spy agency breach.

23
00:00:47,736 --> 00:00:51,386
So what did they take from the Air Force?
Right now, nobody knows.
